[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:Reward for Virtue]
[00:12.93]Why did Hugh's diet not work?
[00:18.60]My friend, Hugh, has always been fat,
[00:23.29]but things got so bad recently that he decided to go on a diet.
[00:29.58]He began his diet a week ago.
[00:32.92]First of all, he wrote out a long list of all the foods which were forbidden.
[00:40.19]The list included most of the things Hugh loves:
[00:44.37]butter, potatoes, rice, beer, milk, chocolate, and sweets.
[00:52.28]Yesterday I paid him a visit.
[00:55.57]I rang the bell and was not surprised to see that Hugh was still as fat as ever.
[01:03.27]He led me into his room and hurriedly hid a large parcel under his desk.
[01:10.46]It was obvious that he was very embarrassed.
[01:14.72]When I asked him what he was doing,
[01:17.71]he smiled guiltily and then put the parcel on the desk.
[01:23.37]He explained that his diet was so strict that he had to reward himself occasionally.
[01:31.01]Then he showed me the contents of the parcel.
[01:34.86]It contained five large bars of chocolate and three bags of sweets!
